# Prometheus Gateway — Environment Variables
# Copy to gateway/.env and fill in values. Never commit .env to version control.
#
# READ BY: the gateway only, via pydantic-settings, resolved by absolute path from
# the module — it does not need to be sourced and does not depend on the working
# directory. The repo-root .env is read by podman-compose and by neither service.
#
# Hostnames here are the PODMAN set. Bare metal needs a different value for every
# URL in this file, and they are one decision, not seven — mixing them produces a
# gateway that starts, reports healthy, and fails on the first call that crosses
# a network. Both columns are side by side in docs/local-stack.md, along with the
# symptom each wrong line produces.
#
# Nothing the gateway needs to start may live only in a shell. A restart from a
# terminal without those exports is what this file exists to survive.

# ── JWT / Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT a URL to make reachable: an issuer is an identifier and is never fetched.
# It must equal, string for string, the `iss` claim the running auth-service puts
# in its tokens (AUTH_JWT_ISSUER in auth-service/.env). A mismatch is reported as
# `401 Token signature validation failed`, so the message points at the key while
# the cause is this line. Decode a live token to see the truth.
JWT_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com
JWT_AUDIENCE=prometheus-gateway

# Key source: set ONE of the following
# For production with auth-service: use JWKS (zero-downtime key rotation)
# JWT_JWKS_URL=http://auth-service:9000/.well-known/jwks.json
# For standalone dev without auth-service: use static public key file
JWT_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/jwt_public_key.pem

JWT_CLOCK_SKEW_SECONDS=30

# Token revocation via Redis (optional; omit to disable revocation checks)
# JWT_REVOCATION_REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
# JWT_REVOCATION_STRICT=true   # fail-closed when Redis is unavailable

# ── Admin dashboard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three are required together — the gateway refuses to start when the flag is
# on and either of the others is blank, which is deliberate: a loud refusal beats
# a gateway that comes up healthy and serves zero models.
#
# ADMIN_DASHBOARD_ENABLED also gates manager_sync, so without it the catalog is
# empty and every /admin/api/* path is a 404.
#
# AUTH_SERVICE_ADMIN_API_KEY is the gateway's own service credential for
# auth-service's admin router and must match AUTH_ADMIN_API_KEY there. It is not
# how anyone logs in — the dashboard login goes through AUTH_SERVICE_TOKEN_URL
# below. A mismatch therefore lets you log in and leaves Users, Nodes, Instances
# and the Playground empty, because all four are built from data auth-service
# holds. It is not recoverable if lost; regenerate on both sides.
# ADMIN_DASHBOARD_ENABLED=true
# AUTH_SERVICE_ADMIN_URL=https://auth-service:9000/admin
# AUTH_SERVICE_ADMIN_API_KEY=<must match auth-service's own AUTH_ADMIN_API_KEY>

# The dashboard login proxies to this server-side, so the browser never makes a
# cross-origin call. Unreachable here means the login page itself cannot
# authenticate — and note the login is exempt from JWT validation, so a broken
# JWT_JWKS_URL leaves login working while every other call 500s.
# AUTH_SERVICE_TOKEN_URL=https://auth-service:9000/oauth2/token
# AUTH_SERVICE_SHARE_URL=https://auth-service:9000/share
# AUTH_SERVICE_TLS_VERIFY=false   # self-signed cert in the Podman stack

# ── llama.cpp backend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LLAMA_CPP_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8080

# ── Observability ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- TLS / CA bundle (RHEL) -------------------------------------------------
# When deploying on RHEL behind a corporate TLS interception, set one or both
# of the following so HTTP clients in the codebase verify using the host bundle.
# `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE` is respected by `requests`; `SSL_CERT_FILE` is used by
# httpx/truststore to build an SSLContext. Point both to the same bundle.
# Example (RHEL default):
# REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE=/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt
# SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt

# ── Telemetry identity — RM-94 ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are NOT settings and do not belong in this file: the OpenTelemetry SDK
# reads them from the process environment, while this file is parsed by
# pydantic-settings and never reaches os.environ. Putting them here looks right
# and does nothing — measured, after doing exactly that in RM-93.
#
# Export them where the process is started instead. podman-compose.yml already
# does for the container path; for bare-metal:
#
#   export OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=gateway
#   export OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=service.namespace=prometheus-inference-platform,argus.component.role=api,deployment.environment.name=bare-metal
#   export OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318   # Argus's collector
#
# Unset endpoint means export nowhere, deliberately — there is no default.
